    "referrals": [
      "POL-RD-09(4) billing integrity: the SGD 3.20 'Bukit Merah Central westbound' ERP line was charged for a gantry this vehicle did not cross (fare_breakdown marks it on_optimal_route: false, optimal_route_erp_sgd is 0.00, and the driver's own statement concedes he did not pass it); refunded in full as a standalone correction and referred for billing-integrity review."
    ],
    "confidence": 0.9,
    "explanation": "Both of you agree on the frame, and it is the frame that decides the case. This was an UPFRONT_QUOTE trip: the fare_breakdown fixes fare_model as UPFRONT_QUOTE with quoted_fare_sgd 22.00, and the total charged is 25.20 — the 22.00 quote plus one single SGD 3.20 line for the 'Bukit Merah Central westbound' gantry, and nothing else. Under POL-RD-11 the distance and time charges were locked at booking, so the 3.5 km / 28.00% excess the trace records buys the rider no distance-or-time refund; POL-RD-02 does not run on an upfront fare, and no one has claimed otherwise. The only live question is whether the 3.20 ERP line was properly chargeable, and it was not.\n\nThe passing-through question: POL-RD-09(4) makes a charge line for a gantry the trace never passes a billing-integrity failure, refunded in full as a standalone correction whether or not a deviation exists. Three things establish that the vehicle did not cross this gantry. The fare_breakdown's own entry carries on_optimal_route: false; the trip_record's stored optimal route ('via Alexandra Terrace and Keppel Basin Road') carries optimal_route_erp_sgd 0.00, i.e. no ERP on the route actually booked; and the driver's own filed statement says, in his words, that he 'did not see or pass the gantry named on the receipt.' That is an admission against the speaker's own interest — a driver does not concede a charge that is good money without reason — and it decides the crossing. The rider's phantom-charge claim is therefore sustained, and the driver's contrary submission that the correction is 'not made out' is rejected: it rests on the absence of a proximity computation in the derived facts while overlooking the driver's own concession on the record.\n\nWhy this is a money ruling and not an escalation. The driver invites a terminal POL-RD-10 escalation on the footing that the ledger and the driver's note are 'mutually contradictory evidence of comparable strength' under POL-RD-10(7). They are not contradictory at all — the driver's statement agrees the gantry was not passed, so it corroborates the rider rather than fighting the ledger, and there is no genuine equipoise for a reviewer to break. POL-RD-10(8) is expressly carved out where the only unmatched line is one refunded under POL-RD-09(4), which is exactly this line. POL-RD-10(3) does not fire because the GPS trace is unimpaired (169 fixes, 100% coverage, max_gap_sec 0.0 — POL-RD-07 is not engaged); POL-RD-10(2) and (4) do not fire because trip_record, gps_trace and fare_breakdown all carry TRP-09114 and the timestamps run forward; and POL-RD-10(5) does not fire because no exculpatory clause has been invoked by either side against a missing or out-of-window artifact.\n\nOn the remaining arguments, most of which we accept and none of which changes the money: the rider is right that the deviation is not MATERIAL (3.50 km and 28.00% fall below both the 8.0 km and 50% gates of POL-RD-01), so the POL-RD-06 driver_profile check is not engaged — and in any event the two citable counters show 0 deviation flags over 610 completed trips in the trailing 90 days, so there is no pattern, no FULL_REFUND uplift on distance and no driver-conduct referral. The rider is also right that POL-RD-03 cannot exonerate the longer route: the only advisory in the bundle, EV-ADVIS-09114-01, is MISSING with issue code MISSING_ARTIFACT and weight 0.0, which carries no fact and is citable only for its absence — and because the ruling does not rest on it, it does not cap or drag confidence. The rider is right that POL-RD-04 is unavailable: the single chat message (11:53) is a question about the fare, not an instruction to go anywhere, it names no road or place, and its waypoint_hint is null, so the corroboration test cannot be run and the clause does nothing for either side. Finally, no driver compensation is due: the distance charged (16.0 km) matches the unbilled distance on the trace, so there is no shortfall to pay under POL-RD-04's compensation limb.\n\nThe arithmetic: charged_total 25.20; properly chargeable quoted fare plus pass-throughs 22.00 (the optimal route carries 0.00 ERP, so no ERP is properly chargeable); refund 3.20, which is the whole contested amount, rounded up to the nearest SGD 0.05 (it is already on the step). Because the entire contested sum is returned to the filing party, the outcome is FULL_REFUND.\n\nConfidence: the deciding artifacts — the fare_breakdown and the trip_record at weight 1.0, with the clean GPS trace — support the ruling at full weight, and the driver's admission is consistent with them; the cap is 1.0, and we rule at 0.90."
  },
